---
export const prerender = true;
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const heraImage = "https://pub-a33abfbc3135413881a1d8eb86543559.r2.dev/heroes/hera.webp";
---

<Base
  title="Hera Guide | Motto Immortal"
  description="In-depth visual guide for Hera in Motto Immortal. Charm mechanics, Sovereign Domain, build priorities, team synergies, and PvP strategy."
>
  <div class="hg-page">

    <!-- HERO HEADER -->
    <header class="hg-hero-header">
      <div class="hg-header-inner">
        <div class="hg-header-text">
          <div class="hg-eyebrow">Motto Immortal - Hero Guide</div>
          <h1 class="hg-hero-name">Hera</h1>
          <p class="hg-hero-title">Patron Goddess of Vows and Marriage</p>
          <div class="hg-badge-row">
            <span class="hg-badge hg-badge--faction">Starglint</span>
            <span class="hg-badge hg-badge--class">Support</span>
            <span class="hg-badge hg-badge--rarity">Legendary</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div
          class="hg-portrait"
          style={`background-image:url(${heraImage});`}
          role="img"
          aria-label="Hera hero portrait"
        ></div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="hg-wrap">

      <!-- QUICK VERDICT (feedback top request) -->
      <div class="hg-verdict-box">
        <div class="hg-verdict-label">Quick Verdict</div>
        <p class="hg-verdict-text">
          Hera excels as a control-oriented disruptor with exceptional charm mechanics and scaling domain utility.
          Best suited for coordinated PvP teams and slower tempo fights, but weaker into high Control RES or burst-first compositions.
        </p>
        <div class="hg-ratings-grid">
          <div class="hg-rating-cell hg-rating--s">
            <span class="hg-rating-mode">PvP</span>
            <span class="hg-rating-tier">S</span>
          </div>
          <div class="hg-rating-cell hg-rating--a">
            <span class="hg-rating-mode">PvE</span>
            <span class="hg-rating-tier">A</span>
          </div>
          <div class="hg-rating-cell hg-rating--b">
            <span class="hg-rating-mode">F2P</span>
            <span class="hg-rating-tier">B</span>
          </div>
          <div class="hg-rating-cell hg-rating--s">
            <span class="hg-rating-mode">Late Game</span>
            <span class="hg-rating-tier">S</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hg-legend-strip">
          <span>S = meta-defining</span>
          <span>A = strong / reliable</span>
          <span>B = situational</span>
          <span>C = niche</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- SECTION: Hero Identity -->
      <section class="hg-section">
        <div class="hg-section-label">
          <span class="hg-section-label-text">Hero Identity</span>
          <span class="hg-section-label-rule"></span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="hg-section-question">What makes Hera unique?</h2>
        <p class="hg-section-intro">
          Hera is a control-oriented Mage built around charm effects, suppression zones, enemy manipulation,
          and tempo disruption. Unlike traditional burst Mages that focus purely on damage, Hera weaponizes
          battlefield control. She disables priority targets, manipulates enemy positioning, amplifies allied
          carries, and slowly overwhelms teams through layered crowd control and scaling pressure.
        </p>
        <div class="hg-pillar-grid">
          <div class="hg-pillar">
            <span class="hg-pillar-num">01</span>
            <h3 class="hg-pillar-title">Forced Enemy Behavior</h3>
            <p class="hg-pillar-body">
              Hera does not simply disable enemies. She forces them to attack allies, move toward her, and
              become suppressed - actively manipulating the battlefield rather than just interrupting it.
              Enemies lose control of their own actions.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="hg-pillar">
            <span class="hg-pillar-num">02</span>
            <h3 class="hg-pillar-title">Charm Mechanics</h3>
            <p class="hg-pillar-body">
              Her charm effects turn the most dangerous enemy into a weapon pointed at their own team.
              The charmed target also gains increased Normal Attack damage, making the effect more punishing
              the stronger the target is.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="hg-pillar">
            <span class="hg-pillar-num">03</span>
            <h3 class="hg-pillar-title">Domain Control</h3>
            <p class="hg-pillar-body">
              A persistent zoning field covers the friendly half of the battlefield from battle start.
              Enemies entering it are suppressed once. Hera gains stacking Energy Regen and Damage Reduction
              inside the domain over time.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="hg-pillar">
            <span class="hg-pillar-num">04</span>
            <h3 class="hg-pillar-title">Carry Amplification</h3>
            <p class="hg-pillar-body">
              Hera increases ATK Speed and ATK for allied carries, creating a dual-axis team role: she
              simultaneously disrupts the enemy carry while accelerating the friendly carry.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- SECTION: Core Role -->
      <section class="hg-section">
        <div class="hg-section-label">
          <span class="hg-section-label-text">Core Role</span>
          <span class="hg-section-label-rule"></span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="hg-section-question">Is Hera a Support or a Control Mage?</h2>
        <p class="hg-section-intro">
          Hera is a hybrid. She does not fit neatly into either category. Her value comes from three
          overlapping functions that reinforce each other in extended fights.
        </p>
        <div class="hg-role-pair">
          <div class="hg-role-option hg-role-option--primary">
            <div class="hg-role-rank">Primary Role</div>
            <h3 class="hg-role-name">Control Mage</h3>
            <p class="hg-role-body">
              Charm, Suppression, Obsession, and Control RES reduction form the core of her offensive disruption.
              She makes enemies progressively easier to control through a snowballing resistance reduction loop.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="hg-role-option hg-role-option--secondary">
            <div class="hg-role-rank">Secondary Role</div>
            <h3 class="hg-role-name">Utility Support</h3>
            <p class="hg-role-body">
              ATK amplification, ATK SPD buffs, and team tempo acceleration give her a genuine support layer.
              Self-healing through Obsession adds personal sustain without requiring a dedicated healer slot.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hg-archetype-row">
          <span class="hg-archetype-badge hg-archetype-badge--control">Control</span>
          <span class="hg-archetype-badge hg-archetype-badge--support">Support</span>
          <span class="hg-archetype-badge hg-archetype-badge--sustain">Sustain</span>
          <span class="hg-archetype-badge hg-archetype-badge--hybrid">Hybrid</span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- SECTION: Strengths & Weaknesses -->
      <section class="hg-section">
        <div class="hg-section-label">
          <span class="hg-section-label-text">Strengths and Weaknesses</span>
          <span class="hg-section-label-rule"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="hg-pros-cons-grid">
          <div class="hg-pros-card">
            <div class="hg-pros-cons-header">Strengths</div>
            <ul class="hg-pros-cons-list">
              <li>Disrupts enemy formations through layered crowd control</li>
              <li>Turns the enemy carry into a liability via charm redirection</li>
              <li>Snowballing control loop reduces enemy Control RES over time</li>
              <li>Self-sustaining via Obsession heal, reducing pressure on support allies</li>
              <li>Domain passive provides continuous Energy Regen and Damage Reduction</li>
              <li>Amplifies allied carries with ATK and ATK SPD buffs simultaneously</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="hg-cons-card">
            <div class="hg-pros-cons-header">Weaknesses</div>
            <ul class="hg-pros-cons-list">
              <li>High Control RES enemies can resist or reduce the effectiveness of her kit</li>
              <li>Burst assassins can eliminate her before her domain fully scales</li>
              <li>Teams that ignore prolonged fights bypass her scaling advantage</li>
              <li>Pure offensive builds reduce her greatest strength: battlefield control</li>
              <li>Value diminishes in short fights where domain stacks never accumulate</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- SECTION: Skill Interaction -->
      <section class="hg-section">
        <div class="hg-section-label">
          <span class="hg-section-label-text">Skill Interaction</span>
          <span class="hg-section-label-rule"></span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="hg-section-question">How does Hera's control chain work?</h2>
        <div class="hg-mech-grid">

          <div class="hg-mech-card hg-mech-card--charm">
            <div class="hg-mech-head">
              <h3 class="hg-mech-name">Powerlust Tide</h3>
              <span class="hg-mech-skill">Ultimate</span>
            </div>
            <p class="hg-mech-desc">
              Hera charms enemies in a frontal AoE, forcing them to attack their own allies. This is not just
              disruption - it creates internal enemy damage and breaks targeting flow. The affected enemies also
              gain increased Normal Attack damage, making the charm significantly more punishing against
              strong auto-attack carries.
            </p>
            <div class="hg-mech-effects">
              <div class="hg-mech-effect">
                <span class="hg-mech-effect-label">Effect</span>
                <span>Creates internal enemy damage and breaks targeting flow</span>
              </div>
              <div class="hg-mech-effect">
                <span class="hg-mech-effect-label">Bonus</span>
                <span>Amplified Normal Attack damage on charmed targets makes stronger carries more dangerous to their own team</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="hg-mech-card hg-mech-card--obsess">
            <div class="hg-mech-head">
              <h3 class="hg-mech-name">Fatal Fondness</h3>
              <span class="hg-mech-skill">Skill 2</span>
            </div>
            <p class="hg-mech-desc">
              Targets the enemy dealing the highest damage and inflicts Obsession. The obsessed target cannot
              attack normally, has reduced movement speed, and moves toward Hera while taking damage over time.
              Hera heals from the damage dealt.
            </p>
            <div class="hg-mech-effects">
              <div class="hg-mech-effect">
                <span class="hg-mech-effect-label">Control</span>
                <span>Hard-disables the enemy's most dangerous damage dealer</span>
              </div>
              <div class="hg-mech-effect">
                <span class="hg-mech-effect-label">Sustain</span>
                <span>Hera heals herself for the same amount as DoT dealt to the target</span>
              </div>
              <div class="hg-mech-effect">
                <span class="hg-mech-effect-label">Position</span>
                <span>Pulls the obsessed target toward Hera, disrupting enemy formation and backline access</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="hg-mech-card hg-mech-card--domain">
            <div class="hg-mech-head">
              <h3 class="hg-mech-name">Sovereign Domain</h3>
              <span class="hg-mech-skill">Passive</span>
            </div>
            <p class="hg-mech-desc">
              At the start of battle, Hera creates a Domain of Power over the friendly half of the battlefield.
              Inside the domain she gains Energy regeneration and increased damage reduction. Enemies entering
              the area are suppressed. The domain scales over time, making Hera progressively harder to pressure
              in extended fights.
            </p>
            <div class="hg-mech-effects">
              <div class="hg-mech-effect">
                <span class="hg-mech-effect-label">Scaling</span>
                <span>Energy Regen and Damage Reduction stack the longer the fight goes on</span>
              </div>
              <div class="hg-mech-effect">
                <span class="hg-mech-effect-label">Zone</span>
                <span>Suppression triggers once per enemy when they first enter the field</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- SECTION: Build Guide -->
      <section class="hg-section">
        <div class="hg-section-label">
          <span class="hg-section-label-text">Build Guide</span>
          <span class="hg-section-label-rule"></span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="hg-section-question">What stats does Hera need?</h2>
        <div class="hg-build-grid">
          <div class="hg-build-card">
            <div class="hg-build-card-header">Main Priorities</div>
            <ul class="hg-build-list">
              <li>Effect Hit</li>
              <li>Energy Regen</li>
              <li>HP</li>
              <li>Damage Reduction</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="hg-build-card">
            <div class="hg-build-card-header">Valuable Secondaries</div>
            <ul class="hg-build-list">
              <li>Speed</li>
              <li>Sustain stats</li>
              <li>Defensive scaling</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hg-build-philosophy">
          <span class="hg-build-philosophy-label">Build Philosophy</span>
          <p>
            Hera appears strongest when built for consistent control uptime, survivability, and repeated
            disruption. Pure offensive builds may reduce her greatest strength: maintaining battlefield
            control over extended fights.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- SECTION: PvP & Team Synergies -->
      <section class="hg-section">
        <div class="hg-section-label">
          <span class="hg-section-label-text">PvP and Team Synergies</span>
          <span class="hg-section-label-rule"></span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="hg-section-question">Who should Hera play with?</h2>
        <div class="hg-synergy-grid">
          <div class="hg-synergy-tier hg-tier-1">
            <div class="hg-tier-header">
              <span class="hg-tier-label">Strong In</span>
              <span class="hg-tier-title">Team Compositions</span>
            </div>
            <ul class="hg-tier-list">
              <li>Control-heavy teams</li>
              <li>Sustain comps</li>
              <li>Slower tempo fights</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="hg-synergy-tier hg-tier-2">
            <div class="hg-tier-header">
              <span class="hg-tier-label">Best Partners</span>
              <span class="hg-tier-title">Synergy Units</span>
            </div>
            <ul class="hg-tier-list">
              <li>Carry hypercarries</li>
              <li>Disruption units</li>
              <li>Frontline sustain teams</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="hg-synergy-tier hg-tier-counter">
            <div class="hg-tier-header">
              <span class="hg-tier-label">Counters</span>
              <span class="hg-tier-title">Avoid Against</span>
            </div>
            <ul class="hg-tier-list">
              <li>High Control RES teams</li>
              <li>Burst assassins</li>
              <li>Fast tempo compositions</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- SECTION: Deep Analysis / Final Thoughts -->
      <section class="hg-section">
        <div class="hg-section-label">
          <span class="hg-section-label-text">Deep Analysis</span>
          <span class="hg-section-label-rule"></span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="hg-section-question">Final verdict on Hera</h2>
        <div class="hg-final-box">
          <p>
            Hera does not look like a simple damage Mage. Her value appears to come from destabilizing
            enemy formations, disrupting carries, amplifying allies, extending control chains, and scaling
            through prolonged combat.
          </p>
          <p>
            Rather than functioning as a traditional burst Mage, Hera appears designed to slowly suffocate
            enemy formations through layered control pressure. She is not a hero you burst with - she is
            a hero you outlast with.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div><!-- /hg-wrap -->
  </div><!-- /hg-page -->
</Base>
